    "turn_idx": 0,
    "turn_text": "From the Radio Cafe and the Kivira Coalition, you're listening to Down to Earth, The Planet to Plate Podcast. I'm your host, Mary Charlotte Domondi. This is a program about regenerative agriculture and the many different paths people are taking to fix a broken food system, restore soil and mitigate climate change. On today's show, we're talking to Congresswoman Teresa Ledger Fernandez, who has a lot to say about fires, floods, soil, and resilience and the politics of rebuilding after disaster. That's right after a few announcements. Registration is now open for regenerate 2020. Join us November 2nd through 4th at the National Western Center in Denver for this year's conference. We hope you will add your voice as we co-create a vision of working together to foster restorative systems and implement practices that better serve our planet and our communities. We invite you to contribute your energy and ideas to the conversation at this year's convening, Cultivating Restorative Economies. Go to RegenerateConference.com for more information. And Kivira is filling out their late summer fall workshop schedule. There's everything from biochar to permaculture and erosion control. Get the full listing at kiviracoallition.org slash events. And Kivira is QUI V-I-R-A. Kivira Coalition is working with food producers to draft farm and ranch plans and provide technical support through our Carbon Ranch Initiative planning program. This opportunity is available to New Mexico, ranchers, and farmers directly engaged in the management and risk of producing food using livestock or managing crop and orchard systems. Priority is given to historically underserved farmers and ranchers. For more information, visit kiviracoallition.org slash planning. And we just want to let you know that now is a particularly good time to become a member of the Kivira Coalition. Membership is the best way to support Kivira's programs while enjoying benefits like a 15% discount on tickets to the Regenerate Conference 2022. Additionally, thanks to the Paul H. Johansson Fund, memberships set up until August 31st will be matched up to $20,000. That means joining as a member now effectively doubles your support. These funds will go to support our land and health workshops, new agrarian apprentices, and the New Mexico Coalition to enhance working lands. Consider becoming a member or making a donation today, kyviracoallition.org slash match. And now to our program. We're speaking today with U.S. Congresswoman Teresa Ledger Fernandez, who represents New Mexico's third district. For those of you who don't live in New Mexico, this program may still offer a lot of insight into not only what people are going through after devastating wildfires and floods, but also the challenges of mounting an effective response to those disasters. It's one thing for the federal government to say, we have a big pile of money for those who've suffered damages, and it's another thing to get that money to the people who need it. And as you might guess, the devil is in the details. We'll be talking about that on today's show, and also we'll be providing a lot of resources for farmers and ranchers that you can find in today's show notes. Welcome, Congresswoman Teresa Leggia Fernandez to Down to Earth.",
