  {
    "episode_id": 49431,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/9/49431.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 8,
    "turn_text": "One of the things, I mean, I've been talking to a bunch of different people about disaster response in general, access to resources, the exact things that you're talking about, and one of the handicaps that communities that are not wealthy have had for a long time is that they just can't get access to federal grants because often they require matching funds, namely they'll give you a chunk of money, but you have to raise money privately, which of course biases grants towards wealthier communities that can access private matching funds. And then there's also the question of reimbursement, like they'll say, okay, you can have, even if there's not matching funds, you can have so and so much money, but you have to spend it before we reimburse you, and those reimbursements are often slow, and people don't have the money up front. So all of those are questions that people are struggling with. I know that you, as a congresswoman, can't necessarily solve that with a snap of your fingers because these are agencies. I mean, these are like FEMA and the USDA and other federal agencies. But how do you think about that?",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
