  {
    "episode_id": 49431,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/9/49431.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 15,
    "turn_text": "really want to see local people working on this. And I am impressed with the Moda County Commissioners. They actually had a meeting where they walked through what you need to do to get that certification, right? And that I think is very useful, we need to continue to have that help. And now that you raised it, I'm going to try to think of what can we bring, because there are small business development centers that we have across the state. You know, I'm wondering if we should set up have somebody from the Small Business Development Center, because they will help you, they help you with technical assistance. This question has made me think that we will now reach out to a Small Business Development Center, because once again, what I can do is try to put dots together, try to link people and resources, because they might be able to help people set up that certification. There was a program that the Carson forest has been doing where they have been doing the liniero program under a myerdomo system where they have like a myerdomo who they contract with local linieros they got them certified and they'll pay them $300 an acre. to clear a forest and then those lineros, they can keep the wood, they can give it away, they can sell it, we don't care. So instead of charging people to go cut the word from the forest, we are paying them because it is managing the forest. I want to see something like that. I've talked to the forest supervisor who is now overseeing both the Carson and the Santa Fe, And I have asked the people, what do you think of him? And there is respect for that for a supervisor. And so I've talked to him about that. I've talked to the chief forester about needing to create the economic activity in Malta. And I want to see that happen. And so I will continue to look at ways of bringing federal resources to help with that.",
