  {
    "episode_id": 49431,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/9/49431.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 22,
    "turn_text": "So with regards to the silo, what we have seen is that they understand that that's a problem. And the rural and partners network is intended to not say I'm going to go after USDA funding. It's intended to help bridge those silos. So this is an example of where the federal government is recognizing this and has said we need help, but we're going to have it come out of rural development just because this is a rural area. So we'll have them there. They understand rural issues and go out of it. You hear this administration say a lot. We want a whole of government approach. And that's a great thing to recognize and say you're going to do. It takes a little longer to actually get it done, but that's why I'm excited about the World Partners Network because they're supposed to do that. If you went to Vegas, if you went to where the FEMA sites were, there was FEMA, SBA, USDA, they were all there together and talking to each other and referring. So we are making progress on that. It is not perfect yet, but there is awareness of that problem and the need to do a whole of government approach. The world network partners is part of that.",
